<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Burghausen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Burghausen is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-bavaria">Upper Bavaria</a> on the Salzach river, which forms the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>. Its castle, stretching for over a kilometre along a ridge above the old town, is regarded as the longest castle complex in the world. The dukes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria-landshut">Bavaria-Landshut</a> used it as a secondary residence, fortress, treasury and prison in the 15th century.</p></div>
